    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-2559",
      "problem": "The point $M$ is the midpoint of the line segment $\\overline{LN}.$ What is the value of $x$ if $MN=4x+1$ centimeters and $LM=3x+4$ centimeters?",
      "worked_solution": "We have the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14171842/assets/60e50f27aef61d5a97f9165dab922fa25cd80c114a0b11bbfbcdfe4c0fdf90e9.png)\n\nSince $M$ is the midpoint of $\\overline{LN}$, the two segments $\\overline{LM}$ and $\\overline{MN}$ have the same length. So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}LM & =MN \\\\ 3x+4 & =4x+1 \\\\ 3x+4-3x & =4x+1-3x \\\\ 4 & =x+1 \\\\ 4-1 & =x+1-1 \\\\ 3 & =x \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x = 3\\,\\textrm{cm}$.",
